    "narrative": "The LawDog starting lineup for June 8th is anchored by a favorable matchup against Miles Mikolas, driving high efficiency scores for **Luis Arraez** (66.44), **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.32), and **Matt Chapman** (64.12). These three benefit from a +15% SP skill boost and a +5% wind-out factor in their venue, making them the priority plays of the day. Meanwhile, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core start despite a tougher matchup against Will Warren, as his premium spot in the order (+8%) and high base projection keep his score at a strong 62.94. **Taylor Ward** also clears the 60 threshold, leveraging a +16% park factor in his outing against Emerson Hancock to overcome a slight platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins was the exclusion of **Lawrence Butler**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.10. While his raw metrics are solid, he is heavily suppressed by a -17% penalty against the arm of Kyle Harrison and a -13% platoon adjustment, which pushed him into \"below floor\" territory. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** was bypassed due to a -12% platoon hit against the left-handed Connelly Early, leaving the optimizer to prioritize the more favorable right-handed hitting environments. \n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Daulton Varsho**, whose score of 40.69 is already the lowest in the active lineup due to a tough draw against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez. If **Daulton Varsho** is bumped down the order or shuffled to the bench once lineups are finalized, we may look to swap him for a high-floor defensive replacement. **Cal Raleigh** remains on the shelf, and with no game scheduled for **Will Smith**, our flexibility is limited. Owners should monitor weather reports, but currently, the primary risk remains the high-strikeout potential of the opposing pitchers facing our outfield core.",
